Rebuild after the VU1 recording: only the VU1 code (src/lib/vu include folder on the generated files, not the target).
- ps2xRuntime/CMakeLists.txt: the generated VU1 code (vu1_generado/programa*.cpp) needs src/lib/vu for
  ps2_vu1_compiled.inl. It was added with target_include_directories(ps2EntryRunner ...), which changes the compile command
  of every game unit, so the first build with recorded microcode (the optimize/native stages of a new install) recompiled
  the whole game (~959 steps) instead of the VU1 code. Now it is a source property of those files only.
Checked with a CMake/Ninja test project: target include folder -> every object rebuilt; source property -> only the
generated file. A build folder made before this patch rebuilds once (the command lines lose the folder).

diff --git a/PS2Recomp/ps2xRuntime/CMakeLists.txt b/PS2Recomp/ps2xRuntime/CMakeLists.txt
index 1e7067d..829fa1f 100644
--- a/PS2Recomp/ps2xRuntime/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/PS2Recomp/ps2xRuntime/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -588,10 +588,12 @@ if(PS2X_VU1_MICROCODE_DIR AND PS2X_VU1_GENERATOR_SOURCE AND NOT PS2X_IS_ANDROID
             DEPENDS ps2x_vu1_generator ${PS2X_VU1_IMAGES}
             VERBATIM)
         target_sources(ps2EntryRunner PRIVATE ${PS2X_VU1_GENERATED_PARTS})
+        # gow-native-pc: the include folder on the generated files only. On the target it changed the command line of
+        # every game unit, so the first build with recorded microcode recompiled the whole game instead of the VU1 code.
         set_source_files_properties(${PS2X_VU1_GENERATED_PARTS} PROPERTIES
             SKIP_UNITY_BUILD_INCLUSION ON
-            SKIP_PRECOMPILE_HEADERS ON)
-        target_include_directories(ps2EntryRunner PRIVATE "${CMAKE_CURRENT_SOURCE_DIR}/src/lib/vu")
+            SKIP_PRECOMPILE_HEADERS ON
+            INCLUDE_DIRECTORIES "${CMAKE_CURRENT_SOURCE_DIR}/src/lib/vu")
         if(MSVC)
             set_source_files_properties(${PS2X_VU1_GENERATED_PARTS} PROPERTIES COMPILE_OPTIONS "/bigobj")
         endif()
